% tet_mesh — a body-fitted tetrahedral mesh of a model (a part, a body, a loaded STL/OBJ, a closed triangle mesh)
%
% Usage:      t = tet_mesh(model, size)            quadratic (10-node) tetrahedra
%             t = tet_mesh(model, size, order)     order 1 (4-node) or 2 (10-node)
%             t = tet_mesh(part(), 3)
% Computes:   tetmesh with PartCraft's Simulation settings (curv 0.25: finer on curved faces, thick 1: finer in thin
%             walls, levels 3 of refinement) and prints the counts, the volume and the quality.
% Method:     isosurface stuffing on a body-centred cubic lattice with graded refinement, boundary snapping and
%             interior smoothing (tetmesh.js); order 2 adds mid-side nodes placed on the exact faces when the model
%             carries them (a PartCraft part does; a plain STL does not, so they stay on its facets).
% Units:      the model's length unit.
% Limits:     the surface must be closed and not self-intersecting; size is the target edge length in the
%             interior (curved and thin regions get smaller elements).
% References: Labelle & Shewchuk, "Isosurface stuffing: fast tetrahedral meshes with good dihedral angles",
%             ACM TOG 26(3) 2007; T10 element: Zienkiewicz & Taylor, The Finite Element Method, vol. 1, §8.8.
% Check:      the box 100 × 10 × 10 at size 5 meshes to volume 10000 (to 1e-9), every dihedral angle above 10°
%             (bin/test-craftscript.mjs --lib).
function t = tet_mesh(model, size, order)
if nargin < 3
  order = 2;
end
if order ~= 1 && order ~= 2
  error('tet_mesh: order must be 1 or 2');
end
t = tetmesh(model, size, struct('order', order, 'curv', 0.25, 'thick', 1, 'levels', 3));
q = mesh_quality(t);
fprintf('tet_mesh: %d %s elements, %d nodes, volume %.6g, dihedral angles %.1f°…%.1f°\n', ...
  q.elements, q.kind, q.nodes, q.volume, q.minDihedral, q.maxDihedral);
end
